SEP-17: separator vertices that separate nothing (isolated vertices, or vertices all neighbors
of which are separator vertices) belong to no part after SCOTCH_graphPartOvl.
Build:   ../common/build.sh <tree> 32 (partovl.32) ; lost.c: gcc ... -o lost.32 lost.c (same flags)
lost.32 counts "lost" vertices: part -1 and no neighbor with part >= 0.
Pristine (INFRA/asan/lib):
  ./partovl.32 2 3 - 1     (edgeless graph, 2 vertices, 3 parts, default strategy) -> ret=0 part: 2 -1
  ./partovl.32 3 6 - 1     -> ret=0 part: -1 -1 -1
  ./lost.32 4 4 -          (path graph!) -> ret=0 part: -1 -1 -1 3  lost=2
  ./lost.32 10 9 -         -> ... lost=2 ; ./lost.32 5 5 - -> lost=1
Patched (../build/lib):
  ./partovl.32 2 3 - 1 -> ret=0 part: 2 0 ; ./partovl.32 3 6 - 1 -> ret=0 part: 2 1 0
  ./lost.32 4 4 -   -> ret=0 part: -1 0 -1 3  lost=0 ; all tried cases lost=0.
The first-pass alternative (alt/SEP-17-a, zero-degree vertices only) leaves "path 4 4" with lost=2.
